WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.419
Hello, I'm Westin, your Halifax West High School guide.

00:00:04.419 --> 00:00:09.311
In every subject, students show learning through what they create, explain, and

00:00:09.311 --> 00:00:09.719
do.

00:00:09.719 --> 00:00:12.105
Here is how to read that learning in PowerSchool.

00:00:13.217 --> 00:00:16.936
We begin with clear learning goals and success criteria.

00:00:16.936 --> 00:00:21.616
In math, English, science, physical education, and beyond, we ask: what does

00:00:21.616 --> 00:00:24.737
the student understand, and what can they do?

00:00:25.883 --> 00:00:30.127
P stands for product: work a student creates or completes.

00:00:30.127 --> 00:00:34.640
A math solution, an essay, a test, or a lab report can

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:35.392
show learning.

00:00:35.392 --> 00:00:37.692
The finished work is one part of the picture.

00:00:38.842 --> 00:00:43.136
C stands for conversation: students explaining their thinking.

00:00:43.136 --> 00:00:48.951
They might explain a strategy, support an interpretation, or discuss a scientific

00:00:48.951 --> 00:00:49.436
result.

00:00:49.436 --> 00:00:52.986
Teachers listen for understanding against the learning criteria.

00:00:54.133 --> 00:00:59.431
O stands for observation: skills and learning demonstrated in action.

00:00:59.431 --> 00:01:04.800
In biology, that could be focusing a microscope; in physical education, controlling

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:07.931
a dribble or applying a movement skill.

00:01:07.931 --> 00:01:11.861
Teachers look for the technique and understanding connected to the learning goal.

00:01:13.008 --> 00:01:18.602
FORM means formative: assessment used to provide feedback and guide next steps.

00:01:18.602 --> 00:01:22.707
Students use that feedback to practise, revise, and improve.

00:01:22.707 --> 00:01:25.369
It helps answer: what should I work on next?

00:01:26.467 --> 00:01:33.115
SUM means summative: assessment used to evaluate learning against established criteria.

00:01:33.115 --> 00:01:38.115
Products, conversations, and observations can serve either purpose.

00:01:38.115 --> 00:01:41.486
These evidence types are not three equal shares of a grade.

00:01:42.633 --> 00:01:46.681
In PowerSchool, the first letter identifies the evidence type.

00:01:46.681 --> 00:01:52.531
FORM or SUM identifies the purpose, followed by a clear assignment title.

00:01:52.531 --> 00:01:58.724
For example: C, SUM, explaining a literary interpretation, means a summative conversation

00:01:58.724 --> 00:02:00.788
about understanding a text.

00:02:01.925 --> 00:02:05.423
Completion and understanding tell us different things.

00:02:05.423 --> 00:02:11.198
Check assignment status alongside feedback: submitted work may still need improvement.

00:02:11.198 --> 00:02:15.648
Some classroom practice may not appear as a separate PowerSchool entry.

00:02:15.648 --> 00:02:19.108
Your teacher can explain where to find daily tasks and how to

00:02:19.108 --> 00:02:20.549
follow up on missing work.

00:02:21.717 --> 00:02:24.302
At home, ask: what are you learning?

00:02:24.302 --> 00:02:26.102
What feedback have you received?

00:02:26.102 --> 00:02:27.452
What is your next step?

00:02:27.452 --> 00:02:30.637
If an entry is unclear, connect with the teacher.

00:02:30.637 --> 00:02:33.168
Together, we can support the next step in learning.
